# Copy to infra/.env.dev (gitignored). docker-compose reads it at boot.
#
# AZURE_STORAGE_CONNECTION_STRING — point at the local Azurite emulator.
# The AccountKey below is Azurite's well-known dev credential, documented at:
#   https://learn.microsoft.com/azure/storage/common/storage-use-azurite
# It's the same constant for every Azurite install on the planet — there is
# no security risk in using it for local dev. We keep it out of source so
# GitHub's secret scanner doesn't pattern-match the format.
#
# Paste the literal AccountKey from the Microsoft docs into the line below.
AZURE_STORAGE_CONNECTION_STRING=DefaultEndpointsProtocol=http;AccountName=devstoreaccount1;AccountKey=PASTE_AZURITE_WELL_KNOWN_KEY_FROM_MICROSOFT_DOCS;BlobEndpoint=http://azurite:10000/devstoreaccount1;

# Marketplace (apps/marketplace) — magic-link sign-in + bootstrap seed credential.
# MARKETPLACE_ADMIN_EMAILS is a comma-separated allowlist; only addresses in it
# can request a magic-link login to /admin. MARKETPLACE_SEED_CREDENTIAL is the
# initial ccm_… Bearer credential the marketplace mints at first boot so the
# main CropCard app can call /api/v1/* without manual ceremony.
MARKETPLACE_ADMIN_EMAILS=dev@cropcard.local
MARKETPLACE_SEED_CREDENTIAL=ccm_dev_seed_replace_me
# 'intranet' allows unauthenticated GET on /api/v1/*; 'internet' requires Bearer
# on every request except /api/v1/health. Default in code is 'internet'.
MARKETPLACE_MODE=intranet

# Stripe billing (UC-48 + go-live tiers). Leave empty in dev: /settings/billing
# then says billing isn't set up, every farm stays on Free, and
# /api/billing/{checkout,portal} return 503 billing-not-configured. To test
# end-to-end use Stripe TEST keys:
#   STRIPE_SECRET_KEY            sk_test_… (server-side REST calls; never commit a live key)
#   STRIPE_PRICE_GROWER_MONTHLY  price_… Grower, $10 a month
#   STRIPE_PRICE_GROWER_ANNUAL   price_… Grower, $96 a year
#   STRIPE_PRICE_FARM_MONTHLY    price_… Farm, $20 a month
#   STRIPE_PRICE_FARM_ANNUAL     price_… Farm, $192 a year
#   STRIPE_PRICE_ID              legacy single price, read as Grower monthly
#   STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET        whsec_… for /api/billing/stripe-webhook (e.g. from
#                                `stripe listen --forward-to localhost:5173/api/billing/stripe-webhook`)
# The webhook maps each subscription's price back to the plan. The Billing
# Portal needs a configuration saved once in the Stripe dashboard that lets a
# customer switch between the four prices and cancel at period end. No trial
# period: Free is the trial.
STRIPE_SECRET_KEY=
STRIPE_PRICE_GROWER_MONTHLY=
STRIPE_PRICE_GROWER_ANNUAL=
STRIPE_PRICE_FARM_MONTHLY=
STRIPE_PRICE_FARM_ANNUAL=
STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET=

# Web Push (NFR-06). Leave the two keys blank to keep push disabled — the
# /settings/notifications page then says "Push isn't configured on this server".
# Generate a pair with: node apps/web/scripts/gen-vapid.mjs mailto:you@example.com
# The private key is a secret: never commit a real value. Rotating the pair
# invalidates every existing browser subscription. PUSH_SCHEDULER=off keeps
# the 15-minute alert scheduler stopped even when keys are set.
VAPID_PUBLIC_KEY=
VAPID_PRIVATE_KEY=
VAPID_SUBJECT=mailto:dev@cropcard.local
# PUSH_SCHEDULER=off

# Sign-in mode (UC-17). 'direct' (default) keeps the dev/demo email + one-tap
# role sign-in. 'magic-link' emails a single-use 15-minute link instead and
# disables the direct/demo sign-in server-side — set it in production together
# with a real email transport: EMAIL_TRANSPORT=pingram (+ PINGRAM_API_KEY,
# optional EMAIL_FROM on a Pingram-verified domain, EMAIL_FROM_NAME) or
# EMAIL_TRANSPORT=postmark (+ POSTMARK_TOKEN, EMAIL_FROM).
# The same form accepts a mobile number and texts a 6-digit code:
# SMS_TRANSPORT=pingram (+ PINGRAM_API_KEY). Unset, codes print to stdout.
# EMAIL_TRANSPORT=pingram
# SMS_TRANSPORT=pingram
# PINGRAM_API_KEY=
AUTH_MODE=direct
# Unset AUTH_MODE means direct sign-in only outside NODE_ENV=production; a
# production server with it unset uses magic links, and it refuses to start
# signing sessions without AUTH_SECRET.
# Public origin used to build magic links (and by adapter-node for CSRF/URLs).
# Required in production magic-link mode: links are never built from the
# request's Host header. In dev it falls back to the request origin.
# ORIGIN=http://localhost:5173
# Client IP behind a reverse proxy (adapter-node reads these natively; they
# drive the per-IP magic-link rate limit). Azure Container Apps ingress appends
# the caller's IP to X-Forwarded-For, so XFF_DEPTH=1 takes the right-most entry;
# add 1 per extra trusted proxy in front (e.g. 2 behind Front Door). Leave unset
# in local dev. When unset, or the resolved address is private, requests share
# one 200-per-15-minute bucket instead of locking everyone out at 20.
# ADDRESS_HEADER=X-Forwarded-For
# XFF_DEPTH=1

# Operator-only brake on the shared Anthropic key: total AI spend across all
# farms per UTC month, in USD. Each farm's plan budget (Free $0.50, Grower $4,
# Farm $10, checked first) counts only that farm's spend. Unset or 0 = no
# deployment-wide brake. Production sets 150; recompute monthly as the free
# pool + 0.6 x the paid farms' budgets + $25.
# AI_GLOBAL_MONTHLY_USD_CAP=150
# Ceiling on AI spend across all Free farms together per UTC month, in USD.
# Unset = 50; 0 = off. Past it, Free AI falls back to deterministic results.
# AI_FREE_POOL_MONTHLY_USD=50
